## What a `type: thesaurus-array` instance is

A first-class SIBLING-LIST entity — analog of `iso-thes:ThesaurusArray` from ISO 25964.  A thesaurus-array is an ORDERED collection of sibling tags under a common parent — the sequential analog of the cross-cutting concept-group.  Where concept-groups are unordered facet memberships, thesaurus-arrays carry explicit sequence (sort-key) for cases where ordering matters semantically.

## When to materialize a thesaurus-array

- A parent tag has siblings whose ORDER is semantically meaningful (chronological / size-ranked / authority-ranked)
- The order should round-trip stably across serialization
- Queries against the array need to preserve sequence

Most tag siblings don't need arrays — they're unordered narrower-of-parent.  Arrays are for the cases where sequence carries meaning.

